  "attestation": "General Chemistry Phase 0 (v1.0.2). Reviewed every required item for statements the change touches (version, units/records commands, the mechanical reader, consistency and module time limits, CHECKED.json, asset records and descriptions, attribution): updated PROCEDURE.md, README.md (units relink, records_paths), docs/migrating-from-v0.12.md (relink after a pre-v0.12 plan, record paths), format-contracts/deliverables.md (<asset>.about.json), CHANGELOG and VERSION; the templates, site pages and images, skills/oer-qa, docs/coherence-index.md, system claims and profiles, and the v0.12 scripts sharing qa_audits (check_oer: .about.json is not media there either) needed no change (site and package.json keep their version lines, as at v1.0.1). Code: runner time limit scales with snapshot files and a timed-out run or recheck is a blocking module-failed saying so; recheckByRerun runs once per snapshot; term resolution cached per consistency scan (findings identical to v1.0.1 on a 660-claim course sample, 27x faster; MS7 now 115 s through the runner on the 6,273-file course); mechanical reader changes checked against all 4,980 units of the course: the 37 equation and 23 computation misreads cleared, no new flag anywhere, 24 more links compared, every new skip counted; existing red-team reader tests (r3-r7, genchem-reeval) pass, including S -> P staying chemistry. New lib/core/relink.mjs reproduces the analysis's 4,760 links exactly; records_paths fixes 157 stored deck paths and regenerates ATTRIBUTION.md identically to generate_attribution. Tests: the 36 required plus genchem-phase0, runner, stable-modules, records-layout, redteam-r1/r2/r6-visible, d49, core-obligations, wiring-modules, site-type-assets, ship-lean, site-export (675/675 via xargs --test-concurrency=2, COURSEWERK_FRAMES=installed), then contract-declarations, skills, system-index, job-release one at a time. End to end on a copy of the course: gate 2,130 -> 2,112 (harness) -> 1,520 (records_paths + relink).",
